# Generated from: specs/12-add-second-serial-lifecycle-smoke-marker/requirements.md
Feature: Add second serial lifecycle smoke marker
  As a maintainer validating serial lifecycle delivery
  I want a second deterministic repository marker
  So that the second serial lifecycle item has an exact, documented, automatically verified completion signal

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Root marker has exact bytes
    Given a repository checkout after issue #12 is implemented
    When root LIVE_SMOKE_B.txt is read as bytes
    Then the file exists
    And its complete byte sequence is "smoke-b-213" followed by exactly one LF byte and no other bytes

  @SCN002
  Scenario: README documents the second marker
    Given the same implemented checkout
    When README.md is read
    Then it identifies root LIVE_SMOKE_B.txt as the second serial lifecycle marker
    And it states the complete content is "smoke-b-213" followed by exactly one final newline

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Canonical marker passes deterministically
    Given LIVE_SMOKE_B.txt has exactly the bytes "smoke-b-213\n"
    When the focused live-smoke-b Jest test runs from scripts
    Then the Jest process exits zero
    And the test uses no network, clock, or environment-dependent input

  @SCN004
  Scenario Outline: Marker drift fails the exact-byte test
    Given LIVE_SMOKE_B.txt is <marker state>
    When the focused live-smoke-b Jest test runs from scripts
    Then the Jest process exits non-zero because the complete bytes are not exactly "smoke-b-213\n"

    Examples:
      | marker state                                      |
      | missing                                           |
      | present with bytes "smoke-b-213" and no newline  |
      | present with bytes "smoke-b-213\n\n"            |
      | present with bytes "smoke-b-214\n"              |
      | present with a UTF-8 BOM before "smoke-b-213\n"  |
